Whereas:

— Climate change poses a serious threat to our planet and our health;

— The Government of Canada has committed to reducing greenhouse gas emissions by at least 60% below 2005 levels by 2030;

— In order to achieve this goal, the Government of Canada must invest in sustainable industries and create new, sustainable jobs;

— The jobs of the future will be in industries that produce clean energy, reuse and recycle products, and transition to a circular economy;

— It is in the best interests of the federal government to invest in these sustainable jobs, which will contribute to the fight against climate change;

— The federal government must enact just transition legislation, producing a plan that reduces emissions by at least 60% below 2005 levels by 2030 and creates new, sustainable jobs;

— The federal government must consult with workers and their unions to ensure that any job loss is minimized and that the workers' skills are transferred to new sectors;

